# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` does NOT upload to Cloud Build (ticket 0009).
#
# ## Why this file has to exist
#
# With no .gcloudignore, gcloud synthesizes one that pulls in the root .gitignore via
# `#!include:.gitignore`. Only the *root* one — nested .gitignore files are not honored. Our
# `node_modules` rule lives in `mobile/.gitignore`, so it is invisible to that mechanism, and
# `mobile/node_modules` (~418 MB) would be tarred and shipped to Cloud Build on every single
# deploy. Slow, and billed.
#
# ## What must NOT be added here
#
# `backend/data/decisions.json` is the entire state of the service — committed on purpose
# (docs/decisions/0002), loaded once at startup, no database behind it. Exclude it and the
# container will not boot. It is covered by no rule below; keep it that way.

#!include:.gitignore

# The Cloud Run service is the Python API. It never serves the Expo client.
mobile/
tests/
docs/
.github/

# `sim/` is deliberately NOT excluded. It is 40 KB, `pyproject.toml` lists it as a package
# (so a build step that installs the project would fail without it), and `backend/precompute.py`
# imports it. Excluding it buys nothing and breaks two things.

# Never needed in an image, and the first two are large.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local runbooks carry infrastructure values. They are gitignored already; this is belt and
# braces, because the one place they must never end up is inside a deployed artifact.
*.local.md
private/
